t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"title-wrapper  title-left\"><h2 class=\"title elementor-heading-title\">Our Asbestos Removal Process<\/h2><\/div>\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2febfd5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-udesign_widget_heading\" data-id=\"2febfd5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"udesign_widget_heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"title-wrapper  title-left\"><p class=\"title elementor-heading-title\">At Coastal Demolitions, we have developed a systematic approach to asbestos removal to ensure the process is carried out safely and effectively. <br><br>\n\n<b>1. Initial Consultation<\/b>: We begin by understanding your needs and concerns regarding the presence of asbestos in your property. We then conduct a thorough inspection to identify the areas with asbestos-containing materials.<br><br>\n\n<b>2. Planning and Preparation<\/b>: Based on the inspection findings, we create a detailed plan for the removal process. This includes identifying necessary resources, outlining safety measures, and estimating the timeframe for the project.<br><br>\n\n<b>3. Asbestos Removal<\/b>: Our licensed asbestos removal team, equipped with proper safety gear and tools, carries out the removal process. We adhere to strict protocols to ensure that asbestos fibres do not become airborne and pose a risk to health.<br><br>\n\n<b>4. Safe Disposal: <\/b>All removed asbestos is carefully contained and transported in registered vehicles to licensed disposal facilities, complying with all environmental and health regulations.<br><br>\n\n<b>5. Final Inspection and Clearance:<\/b> Once the removal process is complete, we conduct a final inspection of the site to ensure that all asbestos has been removed. A clearance certificate is issued only when we are confident that the property is safe for occupation.<\/p><\/div>\t\t<\/d